      "role": "user",
      "content": "It cut off right at the end there—could you finish that last sentence and the paragraph?\n\nAlso, I'd like to tweak the section about the meetings. It's a bit dry. I want to capture the *feeling* of the disruption. It's not that they're being lazy, it's just that their attendance is so unpredictable that it feels like this tiny, nagging problem that occasionally pops up and throws our morning flow out of sync. \n\nCan you rewrite that \"Areas for Improvement\" part to be a bit more descriptive? I want to convey that sense of an unpredictable, almost \"sneaky\" pattern of absence that we just can't seem to get ahead of, even though they're otherwise a great employee. I want it to sound professional but really capture that nuance of how it's this elusive issue.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
